# B-TRACE Demo Presentation Script
(Birth Tracking for Registration and Certificate Entries)

**Audience:** City Civil Registry Office (CCRO) staff, supervisors, LGU stakeholders  
**Format:** Live walkthrough (Electron desktop app recommended)  
**Suggested length:** 18–25 minutes (full) · 8–10 minutes (short version at end)

---

## Before you present

### Environment

| Item | Recommendation |
|------|----------------|
| App mode | `npm run electron:dev` or installed desktop build |
| Network | None required — emphasize **offline / local SQLite** |
| Display | 1920×1080 or projector; zoom browser/app to 100–110% if needed |
| Data | Use a machine with **2–3 sample applicants** (one incomplete, one checklist-complete, one verified) |

### Pre-demo checklist (15 minutes before)

1. Start the app and confirm the API/backend is running (dev: `npm run electron:dev`).
2. Log in once to verify credentials (see **Login** below).
3. Open **Dashboard** — confirm charts render (not empty if you want impact).
4. Pick your **hero applicant** (checklist 100% + COLB filled) for PDF generation.
5. Prepare one small image file on the desktop for **Attach file** demo.
6. Optional: export a `.zip` backup beforehand so **Import Backup** is instant if you demo restore.
7. Close unrelated windows; disable notifications.

### Demo login (default install)

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Username | `admin` |
| Password | `ccro123` |

> **Presenter note:** Mention that production deployments should change default credentials. Do not display the password on a public slide if security is a concern — say “use the demo account provided for this session.”

---

## Opening (1–2 minutes)

**Say:**

> Good [morning/afternoon]. Today I will demonstrate **B-TRACE** — our **Birth Tracking for Registration and Certificate Entries** system for the City Civil Registry Office.
>
> Delayed and late birth registration is document-heavy: requirements change by **age**, by **situation** (deceased registrant, foreign parent, out-of-town birth), and staff must produce **official forms and PDFs** that match national layouts.
>
> B-TRACE puts applicant records, **dynamic checklists**, form entry, and **print-ready PDFs** in one **offline** desktop application — so data stays on our machines, not in the cloud.

**On screen:** Login page visible (do not log in yet).

**Key message:** Document completeness is the core — tagline **Document Requirements**.

---

## Scene 1 — Sign in and navigation (2 minutes)

### Actions

1. Enter username and password → **Login**.
2. Point to the **left sidebar**: **Dashboard**, **Applicants**, **COLB BRAP**, **Logout**.
3. Point to the header: **B-TRACE** and **Document Requirements**.

**Say:**

> Staff sign in locally. Navigation is simple: overview on the Dashboard, day-to-day delayed registration under **Applicants**, and a separate track for **COLB BRAP** with a shorter checklist.

---

## Scene 2 — Dashboard and backups (3–4 minutes)

### Actions

1. Stay on **Dashboard**.
2. Highlight **totals** (applicants, verified vs pending).
3. Scroll to **charts**:
   - Applicants by **age group**
   - **Registration status** (Incomplete Checklist, Under Process, Verified)
   - **Applications over time** — change filter (e.g. Last 7 days → Year).
4. Point to **Recent applicants** — click one name → profile → **Back** to Dashboard.
5. Show **Export Backup** and **Import Backup** (explain only; run export if time allows).

**Say:**

> Supervisors get a live picture of workload: how many cases are still missing documents versus already verified. Age-group charts help us plan staffing — for example, more school-record requests for minors.
>
> Everything is stored locally in SQLite. **Export Backup** packages the database and all attachments into one `.zip` — ideal for end-of-day field work, moving data to the main office, or disaster recovery. **Import Backup** merges a zip back without needing internet.

**Optional live moment:** Click **Export Backup** → show the downloaded `.zip` filename.

---

## Scene 3 — Applicants list and search (2 minutes)

### Actions

1. Click **Applicants** in the sidebar.
2. Show **Search** — type part of a name or date of birth.
3. Toggle status filters: **All** → **Incomplete Checklist** → **Verified**.
4. Point at a row: name, DOB, **document progress** `X/Y`, status badge.

**Say:**

> Clerks can find any applicant in seconds. Each row shows document progress before you even open the file — so front desk staff know if a client still owes requirements.

---

## Scene 4 — Add a new applicant (3–4 minutes)

### Actions

1. Click **Add applicant**.
2. Fill demo data (example):

   | Field | Example |
   |-------|---------|
   | First name | Maria |
   | Last name | Santos |
   | Date of birth | (pick a date → age ~25) |
   | Contact | 0917 000 0000 |
   | Place of birth | `Iligan City Hospital, Iligan, Lanao del Norte` |

   > Use **three parts separated by two commas** so the Certificate of Live Birth auto-splits city and province.

3. Under **Conditional document requirements**, check **one** flag (e.g. **Out of town** or **One parent is foreigner**).
4. Click **Add applicant** → lands on **profile**.

**Say:**

> Registration starts with basic identity. The important part is **conditional flags** — the system does not use a one-size-fits-all checklist. If the client was born out of town or has a foreign parent, extra requirements appear automatically when we save.

5. On the profile, point to **Age group (requirements)** and **Conditional requirements** in the identification section.

---

## Scene 5 — Document checklist (core demo) (5–6 minutes)

### Actions

1. Click **Document checklist** (green).
2. Walk through the **steps**:
   - General documents
   - Age-specific requirements (name the group shown)
   - Conditional documents (if any)
3. On one requirement:
   - **Attach file** → choose a sample image/PDF.
   - On **2×2 Photo** (if visible): mention **Take Picture** / crop with white background.
   - On another item: mention **Scan Document** for ID-sized crops.
4. Watch the **progress bar** increase.
5. Pause ~2 seconds — mention **auto-save** (≈1.5 s after editing stops).

**Say:**

> This is the heart of B-TRACE. Requirements are grouped so clerks do not miss age-specific items — baptismal and school records for adults, different sets for children.
>
> A requirement is complete when there is an **attachment** — upload from disk, or capture with the built-in camera and crop tool. No manual checkbox ticking; the system reflects real documents on file.
>
> Notes and multiple attachments per line are supported. Changes save automatically so we do not lose work if the power blips.

### If demo time is short

Skip attaching every file; open an **existing** applicant who is already at 100% and say: “In production, each line would have scans like this.”

---

## Scene 6 — Staff status workflow (1–2 minutes)

### Actions

1. Return to **profile** of an applicant with **100% checklist** (use prepped record if the new demo child is incomplete).
2. Show status banner: **Incomplete Checklist** vs ready state.
3. Click **Mark Under Process** → then **Mark Verified**.

**Say:**

> Document completion is automatic. Only when every required attachment is present can staff mark **Under Process** and then **Verified** — that is our internal pipeline, separate from printing PDFs.

---

## Scene 7 — Certificate of Live Birth (3 minutes)

### Actions

1. Click **Certificate of Live Birth** (green).
2. Show that fields match **Municipal Form No. 102** layout.
3. Point to **auto-filled** name/DOB/place from profile.
4. Fill or show 2–3 fields (parents, birth order dropdown, citizenship suggestion).
5. Press **Enter** once — demonstrate **keyboard navigation** to next field.
6. Click **Save**.

**Say:**

> One structured COLB form feeds everything else — AUSF, certification letter, and PDF positioning. Enter key moves field to field so encoding is faster than mouse-only entry. Place of birth from add applicant flows into address fields when formatted with two commas.

---

## Scene 8 — Affidavits and certification (2 minutes)

### Actions (pick 2, do not rush all)

| Button | What to show |
|--------|----------------|
| **Delayed Birth Affidavit** | Open form → Save |
| **Paternity Affidavit** | Brief open |
| **AUSF (Adult)** / **(7–17)** / **(0–6)** | Only if parents not married; note age-based label |
| **Print certification** | Click-to-edit request person / purpose; signatory dropdown; Preview |

**Say:**

> Affidavits and the delayed registration **certification letter** are separate screens but share the same applicant data. AUSF appears by age when parents are not married; if married, the checklist expects a marriage contract instead. Certification text can be edited on the preview and saves back to the record.

---

## Scene 9 — Front PDF and Back PDF (3–4 minutes)

### Actions

1. On profile with **complete checklist**, point out **Front PDF** and **Back PDF** are **enabled**.
2. On an **incomplete** profile (optional): show buttons **disabled** — tooltip *Complete the document checklist first*.
3. Click **Front PDF** → **Print Front** (browser preview) **or** **Save Front as PDF** (Electron).
4. Click **Back PDF** → **Print Back** or **Save Back as PDF**.
5. If save runs: mention PDF opens in **Edge/Chrome** via the app helper.

**Say:**

> Printing is gated on **document completeness**, not on supervisor verification — so clerks can produce the packet as soon as files are complete. **Front** merges COLB field data with the requirements checklist on the official front layout. **Back** maps paternity and delayed registration affidavits. One data entry path; consistent output for PSA/LGU standards.

---

## Scene 10 — COLB BRAP track (2 minutes)

### Actions

1. Sidebar → **COLB BRAP**.
2. Briefly compare: **Add COLB BRAP**, simpler list, **no age-group step** on checklist.
3. Open one COLB BRAP profile — same action buttons (COLB, checklist, PDFs).

**Say:**

> BRAP registrations use a dedicated menu and a **five-item general checklist** plus a few conditionals — Muslim attachment, child registrant ID, marriage vs AUSF. Same PDF and COLB tools, less age branching.

---

## Scene 11 — Edit, backup, and close (1–2 minutes)

### Actions

1. **Applicants** → open a record → **Edit** → show conditional flags can change checklist.
2. **Dashboard** → **Export Backup** (if not done earlier).
3. Sidebar → **Logout**.

**Say:**

> Edits to conditions add or remove checklist lines — staff should recheck attachments after changes. Regular zip backups protect both database and scanned files. Session ends with logout.

---

## Closing (1 minute)

**Say:**

> B-TRACE gives CCRO a single offline workspace: **track every delayed registration**, **enforce the right documents by age and situation**, **capture scans on site**, and **generate official PDFs** without retyping across forms.
>
> Questions?

---

## Short demo (8–10 minutes)

Use this order if time is limited:

1. Login → Dashboard (30 s)  
2. Applicants list + open **pre-complete** profile (1 min)  
3. Document checklist — show structure + one attachment (2 min)  
4. Mark Under Process / Verified (30 s)  
5. Certificate of Live Birth — auto-fill + Save (2 min)  
6. Front PDF + Back PDF — Print or Save (2 min)  
7. Export Backup + COLB BRAP mention (1 min)  
8. Close (30 s)

---

## Q&A — likely questions and answers

| Question | Answer |
|----------|--------|
| Does it need internet? | No. Local SQLite and file storage; Electron desktop. |
| Where is data stored? | On the PC running the app; backups are `.zip` archives. |
| Can field office merge into main office? | Yes — **Export Backup** on laptop, **Import Backup** on central PC. |
| Who can log in? | Local user accounts (default admin for demo; configurable). |
| What if checklist is not 100%? | Front/Back PDF stay disabled; status stays Incomplete Checklist. |
| Verified vs PDF? | Verified is staff workflow; PDFs only need complete attachments + filled COLB. |
| COLB BRAP vs Applicants? | Separate sidebar menu and shorter checklist; same PDF tools. |
| Camera without internet? | Yes — browser/Electron media APIs; USB webcam works offline. |

---

## Troubleshooting during live demo

| Problem | Quick fix |
|---------|-----------|
| Charts empty | Add applicants beforehand or mention “fresh install” |
| PDF buttons grayed out | Switch to prepped 100% checklist applicant |
| Login fails | Use `admin` / `ccro123` on default install |
| Save PDF does nothing in browser | Say “Save as PDF requires desktop app”; use **Print** preview instead |
| Backend error toast | Restart `npm run electron:dev`; confirm port not blocked |
| Unsaved checklist warning | Wait 2 s after last edit before status buttons |

---

## Presenter cheat sheet (one slide / one card)

```
LOGIN → admin / ccro123
FLOW  → Dashboard → Applicants → Add → Checklist → COLB → PDFs
HOOK  → Dynamic requirements by age + conditions
PROOF → Front/Back PDF on complete case
TRUST → Offline + Export Backup zip
ALT   → COLB BRAP menu (shorter track)
```

